IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-meaning.l4: Chapter 12, ss 464, 471, 472, 472A and 474 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): accounting standards,
-- the meaning of "annual accounts" and related expressions, notes to the accounts, "corporate governance statement", and the
-- minor definitions of Part 15. Lines 6343-6347, 6462-6486 and 6505-6542 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the term; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words ("means", "does not include"; each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- BORROWED TERMS. Where a definition is handed to another Act, an EU Regulation or the FCA Handbook, none of which is among
-- the sources, the borrowed fact is an input: a plain BOOLEAN where a witness can state it, a MAYBE BOOLEAN where the text
-- hands the whole definition over. This part answers the Part 15 minor definitions for the others (PLAN.md section 4.2).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 464: accounting standards
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6345 | (1) In this Part “accounting standards” means statements of standard accounting practice issued by such body or bodies as may be prescribed by regulations.
@ref s 464(1) "accounting standards": statements of standard accounting practice issued by a body prescribed by regulations (src:6345)
GIVEN `the statement is a statement of standard accounting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1167 the body that issued it is prescribed by regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 464(1) the statement is an accounting standard` MEANS
    IF NOT `the statement is a statement of standard accounting practice`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accounting standards” means statements of standard accounting practice issued by such body or bodies as may be prescribed by regulations"
    ELSE `s 1167 the body that issued it is prescribed by regulations`

-- src:6346 | (2) References in this Part to accounting standards applicable to a company's annual accounts are to such standards as are, in accordance with their terms, relevant to the company's circumstances and to the accounts.
@ref s 464(2) The accounting standards applicable to a company's annual accounts (src:6346)
GIVEN `s 464(1) the statement is an accounting standard` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the standard is, in accordance with its terms, relevant to the company's circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the standard is, in accordance with its terms, relevant to the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 464(2) the accounting standard is applicable to the company's annual accounts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the standard is, in accordance with its terms, relevant to the company's circumstances` AND `the standard is, in accordance with its terms, relevant to the accounts`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Part to accounting standards applicable to a company's annual accounts are to such standards as are, in accordance with their terms, relevant to the company's circumstances and to the accounts."
    ELSE `s 464(1) the statement is an accounting standard`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 471: meaning of "annual accounts" and related expressions
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6463 | (1) In this Part a company's “annual accounts”, in relation to a financial year, means—
-- src:6464 | (a) any individual accounts prepared by the company for that year (see section 394), and
-- src:6465 | (b) any group accounts prepared by the company for that year (see section 399).
@ref s 471(1) A company's "annual accounts": the individual and the group accounts it prepares for the year (src:6463-6465)
GIVEN `s 394 the company prepares individual accounts for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 399 the company prepares group accounts for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 471(1) the accounts are part of the company's annual accounts` MEANS
    IF `s 394 the company prepares individual accounts for the year` OR `s 399 the company prepares group accounts for the year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part a company's “annual accounts”, in relation to a financial year, means— (a) any individual accounts prepared by the company for that year ..., and (b) any group accounts prepared by the company for that year"

-- src:6466 | This is subject to section 408 (option to omit individual profit and loss account from annual accounts where information given in notes to the individual balance sheet).
@ref s 471(1) This is subject to section 408 (option to omit the individual profit and loss account) (src:6466)
GIVEN `s 394 the company prepares individual accounts for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 408 the company has taken the option to omit the individual profit and loss account from the annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 471(1) the individual profit and loss account is part of the annual accounts` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 394 the company prepares individual accounts for the year`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): there are no individual accounts for the section to apply to
    ELSE IF `s 408 the company has taken the option to omit the individual profit and loss account from the annual accounts`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to section 408 (option to omit individual profit and loss account from annual accounts where information given in notes to the individual balance sheet)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 471 item` IS ONE OF
    `s 471 the annual accounts`
    `s 471 the strategic report`
    `s 471 the directors' report`
    `s 471 the directors' remuneration report`
    `s 471 the auditor's report`

-- (2): an unquoted company's "annual accounts and reports": the annual accounts, the strategic report (if any), the directors'
-- report and the auditor's report (unless the company is exempt from audit).
-- src:6467 | (2) In the case of an unquoted company, its “annual accounts and reports” for a financial year are—
-- src:6468 | (a) its annual accounts,
-- src:6469 | (aa) the strategic report (if any),
-- src:6470 | (ab) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:6471 | (b) the directors' report, and
-- src:6472 | (c) the auditor's report on those accounts, the strategic report (where this is covered by the auditor’s report) and the directors' report (unless the company is exempt from audit).
@ref s 471(2) The annual accounts and reports of an unquoted company (src:6467-6472)
GIVEN `the company has a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempt from audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 471 item`
`s 471(2) the annual accounts and reports of an unquoted company` MEANS
    append (LIST `s 471 the annual accounts`)
        (append (IF `the company has a strategic report` THEN LIST `s 471 the strategic report` ELSE EMPTY)
            (append (LIST `s 471 the directors' report`)
                    (IF `the company is exempt from audit` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST `s 471 the auditor's report`)))

-- src:6467 | (2) In the case of an unquoted company, its “annual accounts and reports” for a financial year are—
-- src:6468 | (a) its annual accounts,
-- src:6469 | (aa) the strategic report (if any),
-- src:6470 | (ab) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:6471 | (b) the directors' report, and
-- src:6472 | (c) the auditor's report on those accounts, the strategic report (where this is covered by the auditor’s report) and the directors' report (unless the company is exempt from audit).
@ref s 471(2) Is the item among the annual accounts and reports of an unquoted company (src:6467-6472)
GIVEN item IS A `s 471 item`
      `the company has a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempt from audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 471(2) the item is among the annual accounts and reports of the unquoted company` MEANS
    IF elem item (`s 471(2) the annual accounts and reports of an unquoted company` `the company has a strategic report` `the company is exempt from audit`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a quoted definition read as closed, fork F12): "its “annual accounts and reports” for a financial year are— (a) its annual accounts, (aa) the strategic report (if any), (b) the directors' report, and (c) the auditor's report"

-- (3): a quoted company's: the annual accounts, the directors' remuneration report, the strategic report (if any), the
-- directors' report and the auditor's report (no exemption from audit is mentioned).
-- src:6473 | (3) In the case of a quoted company, its “annual accounts and reports” for a financial year are—
-- src:6474 | (a) its annual accounts,
-- src:6475 | (b) the directors' remuneration report,
-- src:6476 | (ba) the strategic report (if any),
-- src:6477 | (c) the directors' report, and
-- src:6478 | (d) the auditor's report on those accounts, on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report, on the strategic report (where this is covered by the auditor’s report) and on the directors' report.
@ref s 471(3) The annual accounts and reports of a quoted company (src:6473-6478)
GIVEN `the company has a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 471 item`
`s 471(3) the annual accounts and reports of a quoted company` MEANS
    append (LIST `s 471 the annual accounts`, `s 471 the directors' remuneration report`)
        (append (IF `the company has a strategic report` THEN LIST `s 471 the strategic report` ELSE EMPTY)
                (LIST `s 471 the directors' report`, `s 471 the auditor's report`))

-- src:6473 | (3) In the case of a quoted company, its “annual accounts and reports” for a financial year are—
-- src:6474 | (a) its annual accounts,
-- src:6475 | (b) the directors' remuneration report,
-- src:6476 | (ba) the strategic report (if any),
-- src:6477 | (c) the directors' report, and
-- src:6478 | (d) the auditor's report on those accounts, on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report, on the strategic report (where this is covered by the auditor’s report) and on the directors' report.
@ref s 471(3) Is the item among the annual accounts and reports of a quoted company (src:6473-6478)
GIVEN item IS A `s 471 item`
      `the company has a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 471(3) the item is among the annual accounts and reports of the quoted company` MEANS
    IF elem item (`s 471(3) the annual accounts and reports of a quoted company` `the company has a strategic report`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a quoted definition read as closed, fork F12): "its “annual accounts and reports” for a financial year are— (a) its annual accounts, (b) the directors' remuneration report, (ba) the strategic report (if any), (c) the directors' report, and (d) the auditor's report"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 472: notes to the accounts
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6481 | (1A) ... In the case of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year (see sections 384A and 384B), the notes to the accounts for that year required by section 413 of this Act and regulation 5A of, and paragraph 57 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to, the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors’ Report) Regulations 2008 ( S.I. 2008/409 ) must be included at the foot of the balance sheet.
@ref s 472(1A) A micro-entity's notes must be included at the foot of the balance sheet (src:6481)
GIVEN `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the notes are those required by section 413 and by regulation 5A of, and paragraph 57 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to, the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 472(1A) the notes must be included at the foot of the balance sheet` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the notes are those required by section 413 and by regulation 5A of, and paragraph 57 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to, the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the notes to the accounts for that year required by section 413 of this Act and regulation 5A of, and paragraph 57 of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to, the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company qualifies as a micro-entity is not known

-- src:6482 | (2) References in this Part to a company's annual accounts, or to a balance sheet or profit and loss account, include notes to the accounts giving information which is required by any provision of this Act or UK-adopted international accounting standards, and required or allowed by any such provision to be given in a note to company accounts.
@ref s 472(2) References to annual accounts, a balance sheet or a profit and loss account include notes (src:6482)
GIVEN `the notes give information which is required by any provision of this Act or UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any such provision requires or allows the information to be given in a note to company accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 472(2) the notes are included in a reference to the annual accounts, balance sheet or profit and loss account` MEANS
    IF `the notes give information which is required by any provision of this Act or UK-adopted international accounting standards` AND `any such provision requires or allows the information to be given in a note to company accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include notes to the accounts giving information which is required ..." does not say what else is or is not included

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 472A: meaning of "corporate governance statement" etc
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6484 | (1) In this Part “ corporate governance statement ” means the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority .
@ref s 472A(1) "corporate governance statement" means the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 of the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook (src:6484)
GIVEN `the statement is the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 472A(1) the statement is a corporate governance statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement is the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corporate governance statement” means the statement required by rules 7.2.1 to 7.2.11 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority"

-- src:6486 | (3) A “separate” corporate governance statement means one that is not included in the directors' report.
@ref s 472A(3) A "separate" corporate governance statement is one not included in the directors' report (src:6486)
GIVEN `s 472A(1) the statement is a corporate governance statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is included in the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 472A(3) the statement is a separate corporate governance statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 472A(1) the statement is a corporate governance statement`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the statement is included in the directors' report`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “separate” corporate governance statement means one that is not included in the directors' report."
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence defines "separate" for a corporate governance statement
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the statement is a corporate governance statement is not known

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 474: minor definitions
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6507 | “e-money issuer” means—
-- src:6508 | (a) an electronic money institution, within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 (S.I. 2011/99), or
-- src:6509 | (b) a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money within the meaning of article 9B of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544);
@ref s 474(1) "e-money issuer" (src:6507-6509)
GIVEN `the person is an electronic money institution within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money within the meaning of article 9B of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the person is an e-money issuer` MEANS
    IF `the person is an electronic money institution within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` OR `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money within the meaning of article 9B of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“e-money issuer” means— (a) an electronic money institution, within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011, or (b) a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money"

-- src:6510 | “group” means a parent undertaking and its subsidiary undertakings;
@ref s 474(1) "group" means a parent undertaking and its subsidiary undertakings (src:6510)
GIVEN `the undertaking is the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of that parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the undertaking is a member of the group` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is the parent undertaking` OR `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of that parent undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“group” means a parent undertaking and its subsidiary undertakings"

-- src:6512 | “included in the consolidation”, in relation to group accounts, or “included in consolidated group accounts”, means that the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full (and not proportional) consolidation, and references to an undertaking excluded from consolidation shall be construed accordingly;
@ref s 474(1) "included in the consolidation" (src:6512)
GIVEN `the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the undertaking is included in the consolidation` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full consolidation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“included in the consolidation”, in relation to group accounts, ... means that the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full (and not proportional) consolidation"

-- "references to an undertaking excluded from consolidation shall be construed accordingly": not included by full consolidation.
-- src:6512 | “included in the consolidation”, in relation to group accounts, or “included in consolidated group accounts”, means that the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full (and not proportional) consolidation, and references to an undertaking excluded from consolidation shall be construed accordingly;
@ref s 474(1) An undertaking excluded from consolidation (src:6512)
GIVEN `the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the undertaking is excluded from consolidation` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is included in the accounts by the method of full consolidation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to an undertaking excluded from consolidation shall be construed accordingly"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:6513 | “international accounting standards” means the international accounting standards, within the meaning of Article 2 of Regulation (EC) No. 1606/2002 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 19 July 2002 on the application of international accounting standards;
@ref s 474(1) "international accounting standards" (src:6513)
GIVEN `they are the international accounting standards within the meaning of Article 2 of Regulation (EC) No. 1606/2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the standards are international accounting standards` MEANS
    IF `they are the international accounting standards within the meaning of Article 2 of Regulation (EC) No. 1606/2002`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“international accounting standards” means the international accounting standards, within the meaning of Article 2 of Regulation (EC) No. 1606/2002"

-- src:6514 | “micro-entity minimum accounting item” means an item of information required by this Part or by regulations under this Part to be contained in the Companies Act individual accounts of a company for a financial year in relation to which it qualifies as a micro-entity (see sections 384A and 384B);
@ref s 474(1) "micro-entity minimum accounting item" (src:6514)
GIVEN `the item of information is required by this Part or by regulations under this Part to be contained in the Companies Act individual accounts of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the item is a micro-entity minimum accounting item` MEANS
    IF NOT `the item of information is required by this Part or by regulations under this Part to be contained in the Companies Act individual accounts of a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“micro-entity minimum accounting item” means an item of information required by this Part or by regulations under this Part to be contained in the Companies Act individual accounts of a company"
    ELSE `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year`

-- src:6515 | “micro-entity provisions” means any provisions of this Part, Part 16 or regulations under this Part relating specifically to the individual accounts of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity;
@ref s 474(1) "micro-entity provisions" (src:6515)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of this Part, Part 16 or regulations under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision relates specifically to the individual accounts of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the provision is one of the micro-entity provisions` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a provision of this Part, Part 16 or regulations under this Part` AND `the provision relates specifically to the individual accounts of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“micro-entity provisions” means any provisions of this Part, Part 16 or regulations under this Part relating specifically to the individual accounts of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity"

-- "MiFID investment firm": an investment firm within Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014, other than (a) a company
-- exempted by Schedule 3 to the Regulated Activities Order and (b) an exempt investment firm under regulation 8 of the 2017 Regulations.
-- An "(other than X)" site (ruling of 2026-11-05, decided here): within the exclusions, the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:6517 | “MiFID investment firm” means an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 on markets in financial instruments, other than—
-- src:6518 | (a) a company which is exempted from the definition of “investment firm” by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544), and
-- src:6519 | (b) a company which is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 (meaning of “exempt investment firm”) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017(S.I. 2017/701);
@ref s 474(1) "MiFID investment firm" (src:6517-6519)
GIVEN `the person is an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company which is exempted from the definition of "investment firm" by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company which is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the person is a MiFID investment firm` MEANS
    IF `the person is an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014`
       AND (NOT `the person is a company which is exempted from the definition of "investment firm" by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`)
       AND (NOT `the person is a company which is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "other than" site decided here): "“MiFID investment firm” means an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2.1A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 ..., other than— (a) a company which is exempted from the definition of “investment firm” by Schedule 3 ..., and (b) a company which is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8"

-- src:6520 | “profit and loss account”, in relation to a company that prepares IAS accounts, includes an income statement or other equivalent financial statement required to be prepared by UK-adopted international accounting standards;
@ref s 474(1) "profit and loss account" for a company that prepares IAS accounts includes an income statement (src:6520)
GIVEN `the company prepares IAS accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is an income statement or other equivalent financial statement required to be prepared by UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the statement is included in a reference to a profit and loss account` MEANS
    IF `the company prepares IAS accounts` AND `the statement is an income statement or other equivalent financial statement required to be prepared by UK-adopted international accounting standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“profit and loss account”, in relation to a company that prepares IAS accounts, includes an income statement or other equivalent financial statement"

-- src:6521 | “qualified”, in relation to an auditor’s report, means that the report does not state the auditor’s unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act;
@ref s 474(1) "qualified" in relation to an auditor's report (src:6521)
GIVEN `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the auditor's report is qualified` MEANS
    IF `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualified”, in relation to an auditor's report, means that the report does not state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "regulated activity" has the meaning in s 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, except that it does not
-- include activities of the kinds in (a) to (i) (articles of the Regulated Activities Order). The s 22 answer is borrowed.
-- src:6522 | “regulated activity” has the meaning given in section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, except that it does not include activities of the kind specified in any of the following provisions of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544)—
-- src:6523 | (a) article 25A (arranging regulated mortgage contracts),
-- src:6524 | (b) article 25B (arranging regulated home reversion plans),
-- src:6525 | (c) article 25C (arranging regulated home purchase plans),
-- src:6526 | (ca) article 25E (arranging regulated sale and rent back agreements),
-- src:6527 | (d) article 39A (assisting administration and performance of a contract of insurance),
-- src:6528 | (e) article 53A (advising on regulated mortgage contracts),
-- src:6529 | (f) article 53B (advising on regulated home reversion plans),
-- src:6530 | (g) article 53C (advising on regulated home purchase plans),
-- src:6531 | (ga) article 53D (advising on regulated sale and rent back agreements),
-- src:6532 | (h) article 21 (dealing as agent), article 25 (arranging deals in investments) , article 25DB (operating an electronic system in relation to public offers of relevant securities) , article 53 (advising on investments) or article 55A (providing targeted support) where the activity concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments (within the meaning of article 3 of that Order), or
-- src:6533 | (i) article 64 (agreeing to carry on a regulated activity of the kind mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (h));
@ref s 474(1) "regulated activity": the kinds of activity it does not include (src:6522-6533)
DECLARE `s 474 kind of activity` IS ONE OF
    `s 474 arranging regulated mortgage contracts (article 25A)`
    `s 474 arranging regulated home reversion plans (article 25B)`
    `s 474 arranging regulated home purchase plans (article 25C)`
    `s 474 arranging regulated sale and rent back agreements (article 25E)`
    `s 474 assisting administration and performance of a contract of insurance (article 39A)`
    `s 474 advising on regulated mortgage contracts (article 53A)`
    `s 474 advising on regulated home reversion plans (article 53B)`
    `s 474 advising on regulated home purchase plans (article 53C)`
    `s 474 advising on regulated sale and rent back agreements (article 53D)`
    `s 474 dealing as agent (article 21), arranging deals in investments (article 25), operating an electronic system in relation to public offers of relevant securities (article 25DB), advising on investments (article 53) or providing targeted support (article 55A)`
    `s 474 agreeing to carry on a regulated activity of a kind mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (h) (article 64)`
    `s 474 another kind of activity`

-- src:6522 | “regulated activity” has the meaning given in section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, except that it does not include activities of the kind specified in any of the following provisions of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544)—
-- src:6523 | (a) article 25A (arranging regulated mortgage contracts),
-- src:6524 | (b) article 25B (arranging regulated home reversion plans),
-- src:6525 | (c) article 25C (arranging regulated home purchase plans),
-- src:6526 | (ca) article 25E (arranging regulated sale and rent back agreements),
-- src:6527 | (d) article 39A (assisting administration and performance of a contract of insurance),
-- src:6528 | (e) article 53A (advising on regulated mortgage contracts),
-- src:6529 | (f) article 53B (advising on regulated home reversion plans),
-- src:6530 | (g) article 53C (advising on regulated home purchase plans),
-- src:6531 | (ga) article 53D (advising on regulated sale and rent back agreements),
-- src:6532 | (h) article 21 (dealing as agent), article 25 (arranging deals in investments) , article 25DB (operating an electronic system in relation to public offers of relevant securities) , article 53 (advising on investments) or article 55A (providing targeted support) where the activity concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments (within the meaning of article 3 of that Order), or
-- src:6533 | (i) article 64 (agreeing to carry on a regulated activity of the kind mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (h));
@ref s 474(1) "regulated activity" (src:6522-6533)
GIVEN `s 22 the activity is a regulated activity within section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 474 kind of activity`
      `the activity concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments (within the meaning of article 3 of that Order)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the activity is a regulated activity for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 474 another kind of activity` THEN `s 22 the activity is a regulated activity within section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    WHEN `s 474 dealing as agent (article 21), arranging deals in investments (article 25), operating an electronic system in relation to public offers of relevant securities (article 25DB), advising on investments (article 53) or providing targeted support (article 55A)` THEN
        IF `the activity concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments (within the meaning of article 3 of that Order)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that it does not include activities of the kind specified in ... (h) article 21 (dealing as agent), article 25 (arranging deals in investments), article 25DB ..., article 53 (advising on investments) or article 55A (providing targeted support) where the activity concerns relevant investments that are not contractually based investments"
        ELSE `s 22 the activity is a regulated activity within section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that it does not include activities of the kind specified in any of the following provisions of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001— (a) article 25A ... (i) article 64"

-- src:6534 | “traded company” , unless the context otherwise requires, means a company any of whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market;
@ref s 474(1) "traded company" (src:6534)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the company's transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the company is a traded company` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
    ELSE IF `any of the company's transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“traded company” ... means a company any of whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market"

-- "turnover": the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services (the text elides something here: "services ...,"),
-- after deduction of trade discounts, value added tax and any other taxes based on the amounts so derived.
-- src:6535 | “turnover”, in relation to a company, means the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services ..., after deduction of—
-- src:6536 | (a) trade discounts,
-- src:6537 | (b) value added tax, and
-- src:6538 | (c) any other taxes based on the amounts so derived;
@ref s 474(1) "turnover" (src:6535-6538)
GIVEN `the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `trade discounts (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `value added tax (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `any other taxes based on the amounts so derived (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 474(1) the turnover of the company` MEANS
    `the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services (in pounds)` MINUS `trade discounts (in pounds)` MINUS `value added tax (in pounds)` MINUS `any other taxes based on the amounts so derived (in pounds)`

-- src:6539 | “UCITS management company” has the meaning given by the Glossary forming part of the Handbook made by the Financial Conduct Authority under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8);
@ref s 474(1) "UCITS management company" (src:6539)
GIVEN `the Glossary forming part of the Handbook made by the Financial Conduct Authority gives the company that meaning` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the company is a UCITS management company` MEANS
    `the Glossary forming part of the Handbook made by the Financial Conduct Authority gives the company that meaning` -- the borrowed answer: JUST FALSE is the Glossary's no, NOTHING means it is not known

-- src:6540 | “UK-adopted international accounting standards” means the international accounting standards which are adopted for use within the United Kingdom by virtue of Chapter 2 or 3 of Part 2 of the International Accounting Standards and European Public Limited-Liability Company (Amendment etc.) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019.
@ref s 474(1) "UK-adopted international accounting standards" (src:6540)
GIVEN `they are international accounting standards adopted for use within the United Kingdom by virtue of Chapter 2 or 3 of Part 2 of the International Accounting Standards and European Public Limited-Liability Company (Amendment etc.) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(1) the standards are UK-adopted international accounting standards` MEANS
    IF `they are international accounting standards adopted for use within the United Kingdom by virtue of Chapter 2 or 3 of Part 2 of the International Accounting Standards and European Public Limited-Liability Company (Amendment etc.) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK-adopted international accounting standards” means the international accounting standards which are adopted for use within the United Kingdom by virtue of Chapter 2 or 3 of Part 2 of the International Accounting Standards and European Public Limited-Liability Company (Amendment etc.) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019"

-- (2): an undertaking not trading for profit has an income and expenditure account where this Part says profit and loss account.
-- src:6541 | (2) In the case of an undertaking not trading for profit, any reference in this Part to a profit and loss account is to an income and expenditure account.
@ref s 474(2) An undertaking not trading for profit: a reference to a profit and loss account is to an income and expenditure account (src:6541)
GIVEN `the undertaking is not trading for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(2) the reference to a profit and loss account is to an income and expenditure account` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is not trading for profit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of an undertaking not trading for profit"

-- src:6542 | References to profit and loss and, in relation to group accounts, to a consolidated profit and loss account shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 474(2) References to a consolidated profit and loss account are construed accordingly (src:6542)
GIVEN `the group accounts are those of an undertaking not trading for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 474(2) the reference to a consolidated profit and loss account is to a consolidated income and expenditure account` MEANS
    IF `the group accounts are those of an undertaking not trading for profit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence follows "In the case of an undertaking not trading for profit"
